+# Story 2.7: Touch-Target Rules (A29 minute-one working rules)
+
+Status: review
+
+<!-- Maps to tracker row `e2-7-touch-target-verification-real-phone` (sprint-status-finlit-v1.yaml).
+The tracker's AC sketch keeps the human hardware-verification half (build on a real phone,
+measure ≥2cm targets) as the follow-up; THIS story ships the code half: the A29 rules as
+enforced GDScript + programmatic assertions. Dispatch note (briefing finlit-e2-7): implement
+A29 as proposed, flag the confirmation ask in the PR body. -->
+
+## Story
+
+As a playtest gatekeeper,
+I want the minute-one touch rules (A29) implemented as enforced GDScript with programmatic
+assertions,
+so that the dominant button, modal cards, and step-progress UI provably meet the ≥160px/120px
+touch targets, the FIND WORK prefix and oldest-damaged-first FIX tie-break govern the dominant
+button, the modal-card button interplay hides the dominant button while a card is open, and a
+touch-proxy exists for small targets — all testable headless, with zero visual evaluation
+required.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+1. `FinLitTouchTargets` (pure `RefCounted`, no Node/wall-clock deps) ships the A29 constants
+   and rules: `MIN_TOUCH_PRIMARY = 160` / `MIN_TOUCH_SECONDARY = 120` at the 720×1280
+   reference viewport, "never below 120px" floor, `dominant_action()` collision priority,
+   `dominant_button_visible()` modal interplay, and `touch_proxy_rect()` expansion math.
+2. `dominant_action(state)` implements the A29 priority exactly:
+   **FIND WORK (unemployed) > FIX (oldest-damaged-first) > BUY/UPGRADE > WORK SHIFT**,
+   with the FIX tie-break = oldest damaged asset (lowest `id`), and no affordability gate on
+   free (pre-paid) repairs — FIX stays reachable even from debt.
+3. `street.gd`'s dominant button derives its action from `dominant_action()` (single source
+   of truth for text, enabled state, and press dispatch), and is HIDDEN while any modal card
+   is open (A29 modal-card interplay: the card's own action or nothing — never both visible).
+4. `FinLitTouchProxy` (invisible hit-area Control, `mouse_filter = STOP`, `pressed` signal)
+   exists and is wired to the one genuine sub-120px target in the slice: the leaderboard
+   "🔄 NEW GAME" button (110px tall) gets a ≥120px hit area with its visual size unchanged.
+5. Every interactive target meets its role minimum, enforced by tests: dominant button
+   ≥160×160, HUD buttons (🏆 ❓ 🐞) and all modal buttons ≥120 (DebugButton 100→120 and the
+   110px reset button are the two real violations fixed/proxied in this story).
+6. The theme carries the shared `min_touch_size` constants (`Button/constants/…`), and a
+   test pins them equal to `FinLitTouchTargets` (single source of truth, no drift).
+7. Tests assert every A29 rule programmatically and the full suite runs clean headless:
+   `godot --headless --path game --script res://tests/test_economy.gd` → exit 0.
+   (GUT is not vendored until e3-3 — per project-context Testing Rules the bare runner IS
+   the suite; these pins migrate with the rest at e3-3.)
+8. PR body carries the **A29 confirmation ask** (all four rules are `pending-confirmation`;
+   each is a one-line constant change if the user rules differently) + "Decisions & rationale".
+
