+## Dev Notes
+
+- **A29 rule text (verbatim, project-context.md §Game-Rules-as-Code — the spec for this story):**
+  "One dominant bottom-center action button, contextual; collision priority **FIND WORK
+  (unemployed) > FIX (oldest-damaged first) > BUY/UPGRADE > WORK SHIFT** [LOCKED — L16 for
+  the FIX > BUY/UPGRADE > WORK SHIFT tail; the FIND WORK prefix, oldest-damaged tie-break,
+  and modal interplay are architecture-run working rules — A29, pending user confirmation].
+  While a non-dismissible card is open, the dominant button is the card's action or is hidden —
+  never both visible. Labels icon-first, **≤3 words**; touch targets **≥2cm ≈ ≥160px at the
+  720×1280 reference viewport (~203 DPI class), never below 120px** — one shared
+  `min_touch_size` constant in the theme."
+- **A29 tags:** `pending user confirmation` (architecture A29 row; sprint plan note
+  "A ruling change is a scoped edit to those stories"). Implement as proposed; PR asks the
+  user to confirm. Also in scope per the briefing: the touch-proxy (invisible enlarged hit
+  areas around small targets).
+- **Current-code gaps this story closes:**
+  1. `_refresh_dominant_button()`/`_on_dominant_pressed()` duplicate the priority chain, and
+     the FIX branch uses "first AFFORDABLE repair" — not oldest-damaged-first (A29).
+  2. The dominant button stays visible (disabled, behind the dim) while modal cards are open —
+     A29 says hidden (never both visible).
+  3. Two real sub-floor targets: DebugButton 100px wide (< 120 secondary), leaderboard
+     "🔄 NEW GAME" 110px tall (< 120 secondary). Fix/proxy both.
+  4. No shared `min_touch_size` constant in the theme; no programmatic touch assertions.
+- **"FIX is always free" doctrine (project-context, locked):** the event pre-pays the repair
+  (`repair_paid=true`), so the dominant FIX action must never be gated on balance for free
+  repairs. The `repair_cost > 0` path exists only for legacy saves (`repair_paid=false`) —
+  gate those on affordability to avoid a soft-lock (a FIX that can never succeed would block
+  BUY/UPGRADE/WORK SHIFT forever), but a free fix must win even at negative balance.
+- **Oldest-damaged-first:** `asset["id"]` is the durable age key (ids increment at purchase;
+  the assets array is append-ordered). Iterate and pick the minimum id among qualified
+  damaged assets.
+- **Modal-card interplay:** hide the dominant button for BOTH dismissible and non-dismissible
+  cards (the dim already blocks it; "the card's action or nothing"). Visibility must be set
+  BEFORE the `_state.is_empty()` early return — the first-launch flow (age → name → lottery)
+  opens non-dismissible cards while state is empty.
+- **Deferred-layout trap (field notes):** a node added to the tree has size (0,0) until the
+  next layout pass — `await reset.resized` before reading the reset button's global rect for
+  the proxy wrap (same idiom as `FinLitJuice.pop_in`).
+- **Work-shift cooldown stays in the UI layer** (`Time.get_ticks_msec()` — wall clock;
+  `FinLitTouchTargets` must stay pure/no wall clock).
+- **Test framework:** GUT is NOT vendored (e3-3 migrates). The bare runner
+  (`tests/test_economy.gd`, `extends SceneTree`) IS the suite today — add unit tests there
+  and scene checks into the frame-driven scene-regression block (see `_setup_street_scene_regressions`
+  + `_process` dispatch; the runner quits via `quit(0/1)`; `check()` counts checks/failures).
+- **A29 label note:** WORK SHIFT label in the current code is "💼 WORK SHIFT" (3 words with
+  icon — within the ≤3-word L16 rule; do not churn).
