+# feat: e2-7 touch-target rules (A29 minute-one working rules)
+
+Story e2-7 (Epic E2, first-to-dispatch per the sprint plan): the A29 minute-one working rules, shipped as enforced GDScript + programmatic assertions. No visual evaluation in this story — every rule is a constant or a pure-logic function pinned by tests. (The tracker's e2-7 row keeps the human half — build on a real phone, measure ≥2cm targets — as the follow-up.)
+
+## ⚠️ A29 confirmation ask (pending user confirmation)
+
+The four A29 rules were tagged `pending-confirmation` in the architecture. **Please confirm these are the rules you want** — each is a one-line constant/function change if any is wrong:
+
+1. **Collision priority:** `FIND WORK (unemployed) > FIX (oldest-damaged-first) > BUY/UPGRADE > WORK SHIFT` — the FIX > BUY/UPGRADE > WORK SHIFT tail is already LOCKED via L16; the FIND WORK prefix and the oldest-damaged tie-break are the A29 parts.
+2. **FIX tie-break:** oldest damaged asset first (lowest id = earliest bought).
+3. **Modal-card interplay:** while a card is open, the dominant button is hidden (cards carry their own actions) — never both visible.
+4. **Touch floors:** ≥160px primary / ≥120px secondary at the 720×1280 reference viewport (~203 DPI ≈ 2cm), never below 120px; invisible **touch proxies** enlarge small targets' hit areas without changing their visuals.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `game/scripts/touch_targets.gd` (new): `FinLitTouchTargets` — pure rules module: `MIN_TOUCH_PRIMARY = 160` / `MIN_TOUCH_SECONDARY = 120`, `ensure_min_touch` / `satisfies_min_touch`, `dominant_action(state)` (A29 priority + oldest-damaged-first, with the no-soft-lock fall-through), `dominant_button_visible(popup_open)`, `touch_proxy_rect()` (floor-sized hit area, clamped to the viewport).
+- `game/scripts/touch_proxy.gd` (new): `FinLitTouchProxy` — invisible `MOUSE_FILTER_STOP` Control emitting `pressed`, wraps a target with a floor-sized hit rect.
+- `game/scripts/street.gd`: the dominant button's text, enabled state, and press dispatch all derive from ONE `dominant_action()` result (the duplicated `_first_affordable_*` priority chain is gone); the button hides while any modal card is open; the leaderboard "🔄 NEW GAME" button (110px tall — the slice's one genuine sub-120px target) is wrapped by a touch proxy; asset-card FIX enabled for free repairs from debt; `_shift_ready()` is the single cooldown source.
+- `game/themes/street_theme.tres`: shared `Button/constants/min_touch_size` (160) + `min_touch_size_secondary` (120) — the "one shared min_touch_size constant in the theme".
+- `game/scenes/street.tscn`: dominant button `custom_minimum_size = Vector2(160, 200)` (explicit width floor); DebugButton 100→120 wide (the other sub-floor target).
+- `game/tests/test_economy.gd`: 295 bare-runner checks (was 241) — every A29 rule pinned, including a real viewport-routed tap proving the proxy's z-order delivery, a negative control (no over-steal), the anti-soft-lock fall-through, and real-label combined-minimum width pins. GUT lands at e3-3 (per project-context Testing Rules the bare runner IS the suite until then; these pins migrate with the rest).
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **Rules module, not autoload:** `FinLitTouchTargets` is a pure `RefCounted` like the other engines — headless-testable, no scene-tree deps; the autoload count stays at 2 (architectural boundary ②). The briefing allowed "a touch-target manager/autoload or a theme/constants file".
+- **FIX vs affordability:** the locked doctrine says FIX is always free (the event pre-pays repairs), so the dominant FIX never gates on balance for free repairs — reachable even from debt (same for the asset card's FIX button, which previously disabled free repairs at negative balance). A legacy unpaid repair (`repair_paid=false`) the kid can't afford is skipped in favor of the next damaged asset — a FIX that can never succeed would block BUY/UPGRADE/WORK SHIFT forever (soft-lock, forbidden by L7). When EVERY damaged asset is an unpayable legacy repair, the button falls through to the other doors (tested).
+- **Oldest-damaged-first** = lowest `id` (ids increment at purchase — the durable age key), not array index.
+- **Modal interplay scope (superset of the A29 text):** the rule says "while a NON-dismissible card is open"; we hide the dominant button under ANY card. The dim already blocks it under dismissible cards, and "the card's action or nothing" is simpler to hold true; the first-launch cards (age/name/lottery) now hide it too (previously a disabled WORK SHIFT sat behind the dim). Flagging as a deliberate extension for the A29 ruling.
+- **Touch proxy wiring:** the leaderboard NEW GAME button is wrapped, not resized — the point of the proxy is hit area without visual change. The wrap defers until the pop-in scale settles AND the card's first layout pass converges (the transient first pass sizes the card ~8x tall from unwrapped labels), with a bounded frame budget so a suppressed layout can never hang the flow. Accepted trade-off: for the ~0.3s the popup animates open, the button's hit area is sub-floor — taps during a scale animation are unreliable regardless; the floor governs the settled layout.
+- **Theme constants are the design surface, not the enforcement:** code reads `FinLitTouchTargets`; a scene test pins the theme mirrors equal to it (no drift). Enforcement is the tests + explicit `custom_minimum_size` floors in the scene/buttons — the theme constants are deliberately not *consumed* by code (that would add indirection for zero behavior).
+- **GUT:** not vendored until e3-3; per project-context Testing Rules the bare runner IS the suite today.
