@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Adversarial Review — finlit-e2-7 (Touch-Target Rules, A29)
+
+- **Reviewed:** commit `f7140c6` ("feat: e2-7 touch-target rules (A29 minute-one working rules)"), diff `4604e68..f7140c6` (10 files, +680/−60)
+- **Spec sources:** `project-context.md` §Game-Rules-as-Code (A29 verbatim), briefing `finlit-e2-7.md`, story `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/stories/e2-7-touch-target-rules.md`
+- **Verification performed (read-only, temp checkout in /tmp):**
+  - `godot --headless --path game --import` → clean
+  - `godot --headless --path game --script res://tests/test_economy.gd` → **285 checks, 0 failures, exit 0** (commit message's "285 bare-runner checks" is accurate; base was 241 checks, 0 failures)
+  - 6 ObjectDB instances leaked at exit — pre-existing (identical at base `4604e68`), not a regression
+  - Measured combined minimum sizes of every `_make_big_button` label via a scratch probe: all ≥159px wide today (narrowest "🎂 8-10" = 159×150)
+
+## Findings
+
+- **The A29 confirmation ask never reached the user — the story's central deliverable is missing.** The briefing's acceptance requires: commit on `finlit-e2-7`, push, `gh pr create --base main` titled "feat: e2-7 touch-target rules (A29 minute-one working rules)" carrying "Decisions & rationale" + the A29 confirmation ask, and **never merge**. Story AC8 says the PR body carries the ask. There is no PR (only #9 merged and #10 e2-1 open), the commit exists **only on local `main`** (unpushed; `origin/main` is still `4604e68`; no `finlit-e2-7` branch on the remote), and the worktree branch `finlit-e2-7` is still at the base commit. All four A29 rules are `pending-confirmation`, and the one mechanism designed to surface them ("each is a one-line constant change if the user rules differently") was never built. Worse, committing onto local `main` puts unreviewed, unconfirmed work one `git push` away from the real main.
+
+- **The story's own "FIX is always free" doctrine is violated in `_show_asset_popup`.** `street.gd:702` still gates the card's FIX button with `fix.disabled = _state["balance"] < fix_cost`. For a pre-paid repair (`repair_cost == 0`) at negative balance, the card's FIX button is disabled while the new dominant button (A29 rule + the locked doctrine quoted in the story's Dev Notes) actively offers "🔧 FIX IT" from debt. Before this change both paths gated on balance, so they were consistent; the change made them disagree. The engine (`repair_asset`) and the tutor (`tutor.gd:127`, "the repairs are already paid") both handle free-from-debt correctly — the asset card is the odd one out. Untested, unmentioned in the story.
+
+- **AC5's "every interactive target meets its role minimum, enforced by tests" is overstated — the modal-button check is a tautology.** `test_economy.gd:953` asserts `big.custom_minimum_size.y >= 120` where `_make_big_button` hardcodes `custom_minimum_size = Vector2(0, 150)` — the checked value cannot fail and nothing about WIDTH or the combined minimum is asserted. The asset-card OPEN/FIX buttons (170×130) are tested nowhere. My probe shows all modal widths are ≥159px today, so there's no live violation — but the "enforcement" the story promises (AC5, Task 5.4) is hollow for the width dimension.
+
+- **The dominant button's ≥160px width is font-metric luck, not a rule.** `street.tscn:199` sets `custom_minimum_size = Vector2(0, 200)` — height is hard-guaranteed, width is whatever "💼 WORK SHIFT" at font 42 measures (197px today; the test prints `(197.0, 200.0)`). The test pins that incidental number; a font or label change silently breaks the test or, if the floor were ever under-run, would only be caught by the margin-free 197≥160 assertion. The actual on-screen guarantee is the Root VBox stretch, which nothing asserts.
+
+- **Every leaderboard open has a transient sub-120px window for NEW GAME.** Between `_open_popup` and `_reset_proxy.wrap()` the proxy is hidden and the button is live at 110px tall — the pop-in tween scales the card (0.9→1.0 over 0.28s, making the tap area even smaller mid-tween), and the settle loop waits for two stable frames before wrapping. Typical gap ~0.3s, worst case the full 240-frame settle budget (~4s) if the rect never stabilizes. On a real phone this window is a genuine sub-floor, tappable target — the exact thing A29 forbids.
+
+- **`await reset.resized` (street.gd:758) can suspend a coroutine forever.** If the popup closes before the button's first layout pass (button freed), `resized` never fires and the coroutine never resumes — the `is_instance_valid` guard in the settle loop is unreachable. Unreachable through today's UI timing (input processes after layout), but the test's own fail-path `_close_popup()` sits adjacent to this pattern, and any future synchronous close leaks one suspended coroutine per open. The codebase's own field-notes idiom (`FinLitJuice.pop_in` checks `size == Vector2.ZERO` before awaiting) was not applied here.
+
+- **The touch-proxy test never exercises real input routing.** `test_economy.gd:1015` calls `proxy._gui_input(ev)` directly. Nothing verifies that the engine actually delivers a tap at the button's screen position to the proxy (mouse_filter STOP, CanvasLayer z-order above PopupRoot, event-to-Control routing). If z-ordering or filtering broke, the suite stays green while the floor silently dies on device. Related: the whole A29 touch story depends on `input_devices/pointing/emulate_mouse_from_touch` (project default true) — it's not pinned in `project.godot`, and no test or code handles `InputEventScreenTouch` explicitly.
+
+- **The test destroys the wiring it asserts.** `test_economy.gd:1009` disconnects the street's `_on_reset_pressed` from the proxy's `pressed` signal and never reconnects. The suite passes only because the scene is torn down the next stage. Reordering the stage machine or extending it would run the street with a permanently dead proxy.
+
+- **The story's headline soft-lock guard has no direct test, and task 5.2's promised assertion is unsatisfiable as written.** The task list promises "WORK SHIFT never returned while any damaged asset exists" — but the implementation (correctly, per the no-soft-lock doctrine) returns WORK SHIFT/BUY/UPGRADE when every damaged asset is an unaffordable legacy repair. That fall-through — the actual anti-soft-lock branch — is never exercised: `test_dominant_action_rules` only tests one-unpayable-one-free, where FIX still wins.
+
+- **The theme constants are decorative; "single source of truth" covers consistency, not enforcement.** `Button/constants/min_touch_size*` are written and pinned by a test, but nothing in the scene or scripts ever reads them — actual sizing stays hardcoded (`street.tscn` 0,200; `_make_big_button` 0,150; reset 0,110). If someone edits `FinLitTouchTargets` 160→180 and the theme in lockstep, the pin test passes and the UI changes nothing. The A29 spec's "one shared `min_touch_size` constant in the theme" is satisfied only as a mirrored value, not as a consumed rule.
+
+- **The dominant button now hides for ALL popups, not just non-dismissible ones — a superset of the A29 text.** The spec pins "while a **non-dismissible** card is open, the dominant button is the card's action or is hidden". The implementation (and story AC3) hides it for dismissible popups too (job picker, buy sheet, leaderboard, tutor). The job picker and buy sheet are themselves the dominant button's action, so this is defensible UX, but it's a behavior change beyond the pending-confirmation rule as written, and the PR that should have asked about it doesn't exist.
+
+- **The WORK SHIFT cooldown is still duplicated, contradicting the "can never disagree" claim.** `street.gd:374` (enabled state) and `street.gd:399` (press dispatch) each evaluate `Time.get_ticks_msec() - _last_shift_ms >= int(...WORK_SHIFT_COOLDOWN * 1000.0)` independently. Same expression today, so no live divergence — but the story's single-source-of-truth promise (AC3, Task 3.1) explicitly excludes only the cooldown from `FinLitTouchTargets` and then proceeds to duplicate it in the UI layer twice.
+
+- **The story never badge-out'd.** Story file still reads "Status: in-progress" with empty Dev-Agent-Record Completion Notes and File List; the tracker row `e2-7-touch-target-verification-real-phone` remains in-progress (the real-phone follow-up is a legitimate reason for that, but the code story itself is done and unclosed); `last_updated: 2026-08-04` predates the 2026-08-05 commit. Consistent with the missing PR: the workflow's "review pass before PR, badge out all" never ran.
+
+## What holds up
+
+- `FinLitTouchTargets` is pure (`RefCounted`, no wall-clock/node deps), the A29 priority chain is implemented verbatim (FIND WORK prefix > FIX oldest-id-first > BUY > UPGRADE > WORK SHIFT), free FIX from debt works, unpayable legacy repairs are skipped, and `street.gd` derives label/enabled/dispatch from the single `dominant_action()` result — the old duplicated `_first_affordable_*` helpers are gone.
+- Modal-card interplay (visibility before the empty-state return), proxy rect math (never shrinks, centered), the two real violations (DebugButton 100→120, reset 110→proxied), and the theme pin test are all correctly implemented; the suite genuinely passes headless with 285 checks.
